    "text": "Service notice for harbor technicians:\n\nStarting May 12, 2033, Mireglass release 8.6.2 will display a \"holdover\" status when the most recent salinity sample is more than 47 seconds old. During \"holdover,\" the panel continues to display the last accepted gate-height estimate. This status does not indicate that the probe has failed.\n\nIf \"holdover\" persists for more than 7 minutes, technicians should inspect the intake screen. However, while dive permit BR-27 is active, technicians must not restart the controller. Note that restarting may clear the status from the panel, but it will not clear a blocked intake.",
